description:
**General Information**

**Type of contract** Fixed-term contract, which may be extended subject to individual performance and organisational needs

**Who can apply?** EU nationals

**Salary** E/F (bracket 1 - step 1) full time monthly net salary: €4,982 plus benefits, for further information see what we offer.

**Role specialisation** Finance and Procurement

**Working time** Full time

**Place of work** Frankfurt am Main, Germany

**Closing date** 15.12.2026

**Your team**

You will be part of the Budgeting and Controlling Division in the Directorate Finance, which is part of the Directorate General Corporate Services. Our Directorate performs financial accounting and reporting as well as planning and controlling activities. It also provides cost accounting, procurement and supervisory fee-related services.




The Budgeting and Controlling Division has around 40 members of staff across five teams. We facilitate the planning, monitoring and controlling of resources for all ECB business areas. We specialise in providing analysis for decision-making by offering comprehensive support and advice to executive leadership, business area management and other stakeholders. We also provide secretariat services to three committees and oversee the supervisory fee framework. Furthermore, our Division plays a pivotal role in implementing systems innovation within the Directorate Finance and provides functional support for the ECB’s procure-to-pay process.




The ECB is an inclusive employer and we strive to reflect the diversity of the population we serve. We encourage you to apply irrespective of age, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity, race, religious beliefs, sexual orientation or other characteristics.




**Your role**

As a Finance analyst, you will:

* develop and maintain analytical frameworks and tools, especially those used for data analysis and compilation, applying innovative approaches and digital solutions effectively to enhance efficiency and analytical capabilities;
* analyse complex data from multiple sources, ensuring consistency and accuracy, and produce concise, coherent and harmonised analysis on different topics;
* help deliver state-of-the-art visualisations of these analyses for decision-making bodies and develop financial models for multi-annual budget and cost projections, including running and maintaining the cost model;
* identify, propose and implement process improvements and advance innovation, data analytics and digitalisation initiatives in the context of both the Division’s goals and the Directorate’s digitalisation roadmap, including salary and headcount monitoring and reporting tools and by automating and streamlining of financial processes;
* contribute to the Division’s analytical work on the banking supervision fee framework, the preparation of financial reports, dashboards and forecasts, and the processing and analysis of financial/budgetary data and headcount allocation (using tools such as MS Excel, SAP Analytics Cloud, SAP BW and Tableau);
* provide analytical support and advice to other business areas regarding the effective and efficient use of resources, ensuring alignment with existing policies, and help prepare corporate performance data and information for decision-making bodies and advisory fora, especially on the planning and management of headcount and related resources;
* support the preparation and monitoring of the salary budget and headcount consumption, carrying out regular analysis against budget allocations and reporting on drivers and variances;
* undertake deep-dive analyses on selected topics, delivering well-substantiated findings and actionable insights to support data-driven decision-making.



For these roles we are seeking candidates who demonstrate the potential for growth, and we will support the selected candidates in their development of the required skills. We actively support professional development for our staff. Besides learning opportunities such as training and mentoring, we encourage and support horizontal mobility after some years in the same position.




The position offers you excellent opportunities to work on a broad range of budgeting and controlling topics, to interact with different stakeholders and to actively share your knowledge within a team to further strengthen its performance.




You will be part of a multicultural team that strives for continuous innovation to make a positive impact on the lives of European citizens.



**Qualifications, experience and skills**

Essential:

* a bachelor’s degree or equivalent in finance, accounting, business administration, economics, mathematics, computer science or another relevant field (see How you can join us for details on degree equivalences);
* in addition to the above, a minimum of two years’ experience (including traineeships) in budgeting and controlling and/or financial planning and analysis, management reporting or a related field;
* proven professional experience in financial data analysis and compilation, and the ability to shape and visualise high-level and detailed data for policymakers via dashboards, reports and presentations;
* proven experience in analysing business activities and related resources to translate raw data into information that can be used to improve organisational performance;
* experience in producing reports or dashboards and in using advanced analytical tools (such as SAP Analytics Cloud, Mendix or AI-based tools) to prepare reports and financial analysis, as well as experience in using corporate activity planning tools and digitalising financial processes and deliverables;
* advanced knowledge of MS Excel and enterprise resource planning software such as SAP;
* an advanced (C1) command of English and an intermediate (B1) command of at least one other official language of the EU, according to the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages.



Desired:

* experience in preparing and/or supporting the preparation of multi-annual cost projections and/or data forecasting;
* direct experience with or exposure to budgeting and controlling systems , especially in providing analytical support for budget planning, implementation, monitoring and reporting in an international environment;
* familiarity with budgeting, financial governance or cost recovery frameworks in public institutions, international organisations or other complex organisations;
* understanding of source-to-pay processes in a large organisation;
* hands-on experience of data management, data forecasting and financial analysis tools.



You engage collaboratively with others. You pursue team goals and learn willingly from other people’s diverse perspectives. You signal any need for change by explaining it and proposing alternative solutions. You analyse complex information effectively and can evaluate different views to arrive at solutions. You know and anticipate stakeholder needs.




You are motivated to contribute to the ECB’s mission, to serve the citizens of the EU as a member of a public institution and to work with colleagues from all over Europe. You are motivated to be part of our team and to develop and use your skills and competencies to achieve the aims of this position.



**Working modalities**

We would be happy to discuss a part-time arrangement for this role.

**Further information**

The contract(s) offered will be fixed-term, the appointment being for 12 months as of the exact starting date of the selected applicant. Temporary appointments may be extended or made permanent subject to organisational needs and budgetary constraints. This may result in a staff member with a non-convertible fixed-term contract being offered a convertible contract in accordance with the ECB Conditions of Employment.




For additional information on this specific vacancy, you can speak to the hiring manager, Dominika Ryzner, on +49 (0)69 1344 5712 between 14:00 and 15:00 CET on Friday, 4 December.



**Application and selection process**

The recruitment process for this position will be conducted remotely. It will include a written exercise, a presentation and an interview.




If you are not selected for this position but are still considered suitable, you will be placed on a reserve list (see step 4 of How we hire), from which you might be considered for similar positions within the ECB.



Find out how to apply for a position at the ECB.



Read more about how you can join us.

**General Information**

**Type of contract** Fixed-term contract, which may be extended subject to individual performance and organisational needs

**Contract end date** 31.03.2028

**Who can apply?** EU nationals

**Salary** H (bracket 1 - step 1) full time monthly net salary: €8,318 plus benefits, for further information see what we offer.

**Role specialisation** Market Infrastructure Project Management

**Working time** Full time

**Place of work** Frankfurt am Main, Germany

**Closing date** 11.12.2026

**Your team**

You will be part of the Digital Euro Service Platform Division in the Directorate Digital Euro, which is part of the Directorate General Market Infrastructure and Payments. We are seeking candidates for three Product Management and Delivery Lead positions.




Our Directorate is responsible for leading the digital euro project. It supports the digital euro governance bodies in steering, controlling and monitoring the project. It also oversees all project workstreams and manages the scope, budget and resources approved by the Governing Council. Our Division is responsible for the functional architecture and delivery of the digital euro service platform as well as preparations for its future operation.




In your role as Product Management and Delivery Lead, you will be part of the virtual solution management team working on the functional architecture and implementation of the epic roadmap for the digital euro solution. You will report to the Digital Euro Service Platform Division’s management team.




We aim to fill three positions, each focusing on different use cases and/or technologies:

* Delivery lead for online payments;

* Delivery lead for offline payments;

* Delivery lead for the digital euro app (with a cross-functional component supporting both online and offline use cases) and the risk and fraud component.

The formal title of these positions will be Lead Market Infrastructure Expert.




The ECB is an inclusive employer and we strive to reflect the diversity of the population we serve. We encourage you to apply irrespective of age, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender identity, race, religious beliefs, sexual orientation or other characteristics.



**Your role**

As a Product Management and Delivery Lead, you will:




* coordinate the work of virtual cross-functional teams of subject matter experts (including functional analysts and technical, business and testing experts) to support functional architecture design and delivery activities in a Scaled Agile Framework (SAFe) environment;
* provide functional and technical design advice for the components within your remit, ensuring that interactions and dependencies between solution components and across epics are identified and managed;
* engage and collaborate with business representatives, vendors and other project stakeholders at leadership level, supporting decision-making as well as the assessment and management of risks and impacts;
* support the solution management function by representing the perspectives and delivery needs of the virtual teams and facilitating effective team-vendor coordination;
* contribute to alignment across business, technical and project management stakeholders and support reporting at portfolio management level as required;
* foster a collaborative and efficient working environment within the team(s) under your lead.



The position offers you excellent opportunities to contribute to the core functional architecture of a transformational payment infrastructure that will serve millions of citizens and businesses across the euro area. You will be part of a multicultural team that strives for continuous innovation to make a positive impact on the lives of European citizens.




We actively support professional development for our staff. Besides learning opportunities such as training and mentoring, we encourage and support horizontal mobility after some years in the same position.



**Qualifications, experience and skills**

Essential:

* a master’s degree or equivalent in business, economics, project management, a STEM subject (science, technology, engineering or mathematics) or another relevant field (see How you can join us on our website for details on degree equivalences);
* in addition to the above, a minimum of six years’ professional experience (other than as an intern or trainee) in payments, applied cryptography, a security-related domain or solutions in the bank-to-consumer domain;
* a minimum of three years’ professional experience in leading or coordinating multidisciplinary teams;
* experience in delivering complex solutions using agile delivery methodologies;
* a sound understanding of the functional architecture and technologies relevant to the position(s) you are applying for, including security, systems integration and interfaces:
* + for the online use cases delivery lead profile, experience in designing and developing payments solutions, with a focus on liquidity management and the settlement of payments;
  + for the offline use cases delivery lead profile, experience in applied cryptography or security-related technologies, with at least two years specialising in secure elements/smart cards;
  + for the digital euro app and risk and fraud component delivery lead profile, experience in designing and delivering secure, high-availability mobile applications in the payments domain, and a sound understanding of payment processing and mobile architectures;
* experience in drafting clear and concise notes and reports, and presenting complex topics to different audiences;
* an advanced (C1) command of English and an intermediate (B1) command of at least one other official language of the EU, according to the Common European Framework of Reference for Languages.



Desired:

* experience in delivering complex solutions or projects using SAFe;
* technical knowledge of the standards applicable to payments, payment schemes or solutions in the bank-to-consumer domain;
* for the digital euro app and risk and fraud component delivery lead profile, experience in risk and fraud management solutions in the payments domain, with technical expertise in fraud detection, risk engines and data analytics;
* for the offline use cases delivery lead profile, experience in developing an offline, or partially offline, payment solution.



You engage collaboratively with others. You pursue team goals and learn willingly from other people’s diverse perspectives. You signal any need for change by explaining it and proposing alternative solutions. You analyse complex information effectively and can evaluate different views to arrive at solutions. You know and anticipate stakeholder needs.




You are motivated to contribute to the ECB’s mission, to serve the citizens of the EU as a member of a public institution and to work with colleagues from all over Europe. You are aware of your strengths and areas for development and know what motivates you to perform at your highest level.



**Working modalities**

We would be happy to discuss a part-time arrangement for this role.

**Further information**

At least one of the contracts for these three positions will be convertible into a permanent contract after three years subject to individual performance and organisational needs.

The other contract(s) offered will be fixed-term, the appointment being until 31 March 2028. Temporary appointments may be extended or made permanent subject to organisational needs and budgetary constraints. This may result in a staff member with a non-convertible fixed-term contract being offered a convertible contract in accordance with the ECB Conditions of Employment.




For additional information on this specific vacancy, you can speak to the hiring manager, Maria Velasco, on +49 (0)69 1344 8022 between 17:00 and 18:30 on Thursday, 26 November.



**Application and selection process**

The recruitment process for these positions will be conducted fully remotely. It will include a written exercise, a presentation and interviews.




If you are not selected for this position but are still considered suitable, you will be placed on a reserve list (see step 4 of How we hire), from which you might be considered for similar positions within the ECB.



Find out how to apply for a position at the ECB.



Read more about how you can join us.
